flowchart TD
    A([Model created]) --> B[CMModel initializeParameters:<br/>class parameters reset to pragma defaults]
    B --> C{init method}
    C -- initBigGridScenario --> D1[100 households, 40 outlets<br/>grid 30 x 30, 8-neighbourhood, closed]
    C -- initUnconstraintedScenario --> D2[2 households, 20 outlets<br/>money 2000, time 24 h, fridge 500,<br/>restock 300, grid 5 x 5]
    C -- initCustomizable --> D3[households and outlets from parameters<br/>grid 6 x 6]
    C -- "initBaseline and 5 other scenarios" --> D4[initScenarioWithOutlets:restocking:on:<br/>100 households, grid 30 x 30,<br/>every class parameter set:<br/>money 200, 2 h, fridge 20, sizes 2..5,<br/>outlets, restock and outlet region per scenario]
    D1 --> E[initializeFoodCategories: 5 categories]
    D2 --> E
    D3 --> E
    D4 --> E
    E --> F[create households on random empty cells<br/>size uniform-rounded in 2..5, dailyNeed = 10 x size,<br/>money, time from class parameters,<br/>MoneySaver and balanced diet by default, empty inventory]
    F --> G[initializePreferences:<br/>shuffled households are sent preferMeatAndDairy,<br/>preferStapleAndProcessedFood, preferBalancedDiet in turn,<br/>then storeFoodForTheFirstDay: dailyNeed meals<br/>of the most preferred category, outside fridge]
    G --> H[initializeSubstitutionList: same chain for all]
    H --> I[initializeStrategies:<br/>shuffled agents, first 50 percent MoneySaver,<br/>the rest TimeSaver]
    I --> J[create outlets on random empty cells,<br/>only in the scenario's region if it has one<br/>prices 5 per meal, initial restock]
    J --> K[every household knows every outlet]
    K --> Z([ready, step 0])
